theory.intro:
The **domain** is every allowed input $x$; the **range** is every output $y$. On a graph the domain is the shadow on the $x$-axis, the range the shadow on the $y$-axis. Write each as an **inequality** and in **interval notation**.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-1.4,0)--(5.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.1)--(0,4.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[gray,dashed] (1,1)--(1,0);
\draw[gray,dashed] (1,1)--(0,1);
\draw[gray,dashed] (4,3.5)--(4,0);
\draw[gray,dashed] (4,3.5)--(0,3.5);
\draw[thick,domain=1:4,smooth,samples=60,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1+0.2778*(\x-1)*(\x-1)});
\fill[black] (1,1) circle (2.5pt);
\fill[black] (4,3.5) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[blue,line width=2pt] (1,0)--(4,0);
\draw[red,line width=2pt] (0,1)--(0,3.5);
\node[below] at (1,-0.12) {$a$};
\node[below] at (4,-0.12) {$b$};
\node[left] at (-0.14,1) {$c$};
\node[left] at (-0.14,3.5) {$d$};
\node[blue,below] at (2.5,-0.85) {domain};
\node[red,rotate=90] at (-1.1,2.25) {range};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

facts:
An open endpoint $\circ$ is **excluded**, shown by $<$ or $>$ and a round bracket.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-1.4,0)--(5.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.1)--(0,4.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[gray,dashed] (1,1)--(1,0);
\draw[gray,dashed] (4,3.5)--(4,0);
\draw[thick,domain=1:4,smooth,samples=60,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1+0.2778*(\x-1)*(\x-1)});
\fill[black] (1,1) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[thick,fill=white] (4,3.5) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[blue,line width=2pt] (1,0)--(4,0);
\fill[blue] (1,0) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[blue,line width=1pt,fill=white] (4,0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below] at (1,-0.16) {$a$};
\node[below] at (4,-0.16) {$b$};
\node at (1.9,3.2) {$a \leq x < b$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An arrow means the graph continues forever, so the domain or range runs to $-\infty$ or $\infty$, always written with a round bracket.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-1.4,0)--(5.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.1)--(0,4.7) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[gray,dashed] (1,1)--(1,0);
\draw[thick,->,domain=1:4.3,smooth,samples=60,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1+0.2778*(\x-1)*(\x-1)});
\fill[black] (1,1) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[blue,line width=2pt,->] (1,0)--(4.9,0);
\fill[blue] (1,0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below] at (1,-0.16) {$a$};
\node at (1.9,3.2) {$x \geq a$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

